@*
    OdsRecordTable — the sortable / expandable / editable record table
    (Odyssey Design System · components/RecordTable).

    The table behind every admin/ledger screen (Transaction tags, Contacts,
    Currencies, Exchange rates, Users). It owns ALL the view machinery so a page
    only declares its Columns and supplies the detail / edit panels:

      • sortable headers (uncontrolled — give DefaultSort; the table sorts via
        each column's SortValue), rendered as OdsSortHeader cells
      • click a row (or a "View details" action) to expand it into a read-only
        RenderDetail panel — accordion by default, MultiOpen to keep several open
      • an inline RenderEdit panel that swaps in over the detail; rows being
        edited never auto-collapse on sort
      • a trailing actions cell: the more_vert overflow menu (an OdsMenu built
        from Actions(row, ctx)) + the expand chevron
      • the loading / refetching / error / empty states, delegated to OdsListStatus
        (pass Loading + Error + HasFilters rather than assembling them per page)

    INTERACTIVE CELLS. A row click whose target sits inside an interactive element (input, button,
    a, select, textarea, label, [role=switch], [role=menuitem]) is ignored, so a switch or a link in
    a cell never expands its row. The click target is not part of Blazor's MouseEventArgs, so a
    capture-phase listener (odsRecTrackClicks) records it on the table and the row handler asks.

    FOCUS. The chevron and a row click leave focus where it is, so the aria-expanded control can be
    pressed again to undo. The row menu's View details moves focus into the detail panel (its first
    focusable element, else the panel itself) and its Collapse returns it to the chevron, because the
    menu item unmounts with its popover. StartEdit moves focus to
    the edit row's first field after the row menu has closed and restored its own focus; ending an
    edit (Save, Cancel, or a caller action through OdsRecordEditContext.Done) returns it to the row's
    menu trigger, whose id OdsRecordActionContext.MenuTriggerId hands to a dialog's ReturnFocusToId.

    EXPANSION IS OPT-IN. A table given neither RenderDetail nor RenderEdit has
    nothing to expand into, so it renders no chevron, ignores row clicks and
    drops the pointer cursor — a surface whose columns already show every field
    (Currencies, Exchange rates, tag admin, Files) is a flat table, not a
    collapsed one. Rows that DO expand are unchanged.

    CAPTION, ROW HEADER, BUSY ROW (issue #451). Caption renders a <caption> (CaptionHidden keeps it
    visually hidden); RowHeader names one column key whose body cells render as <th scope="row">.
    RowBusy(row) marks a row whose save is in flight: its actions cell shows a small spinner named
    "Saving {RowLabel}" INSTEAD of the menu. If focus was on that row's menu when it went busy, it
    moves to the row header cell (the RowHeader column, else the first column — focusable with
    tabindex=-1 only when RowBusy is given) and back to the menu trigger once the row is idle.

    NO EMPTY MENUS. A row whose Actions yields no available item gets no menu trigger at all.

    ROW NAMES. RowLabel(row) names each record for its chevron — "Show details for {label}" /
    "Hide details for {label}" — and points the chevron's aria-controls at a role="group" labelled
    "Details for {label}" inside the panel. Without it the toggle reads "Expand row" / "Collapse row".

    Conceptually a MudTable with sort labels + expandable detail rows; built on
    raw table markup (like OdsCollapsible) because the accordion + inline-edit +
    saved-flash state machine is beyond MudTable's declarative model. Pairs with
    the OdsSortHeader / OdsMetaTile atoms and OdsMenu when you hand-roll a table.
*@

@typeparam TRow

@* The refetch bar sits above the table rather than inside it — a <tr> cannot carry it, and the
   ARIA on it is owned once by OdsListStatus. *@
@if (Refetching && !Loading && !Error)
{
    <OdsListStatus Refetching="true" Noun="@Noun" BarClass="@BarClass" />
}
@* The skeleton rows below are aria-hidden decoration, so the first fetch is announced here
   instead — otherwise swapping the centered spinner (which carried role="status") for skeleton
   rows would leave a screen-reader user with silence while the table loads. *@
@if (Loading)
{
    <div class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading @Noun…</div>
}
@* A record table is as wide as its columns need, which on a phone is wider than the page; the
   wrapper scrolls it in place instead of pushing the whole page sideways. No tab stop of its own:
   every row carries focusable controls, and focusing one scrolls it into view. *@
<div class="odc-rec-scroll">
    <table id="@_tableId" class="odc-rec @(CanExpand ? null : "odc-rec-flat") @Class" aria-label="@AriaLabel" aria-busy="@(Loading ? "true" : "false")">
        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Caption))
        {
            <caption class="@(CaptionHidden ? "odc-sr-only" : "odc-table-caption")">@Caption</caption>
        }
        <thead>
            <tr>
                @if (Leading is not null)
                {
                    <th scope="col" style="width:36px"></th>
                }
                @foreach (var col in Columns)
                {
                    @if (col.Sortable)
                    {
                        <OdsSortHeader SortKey="@col.Key" Sort="@EffectiveSort" OnSort="ToggleSort" Align="@col.Align"
                                       Style="@(col.Width is not null ? $"width:{col.Width}" : null)">
                            @HeaderFor(col)
                        </OdsSortHeader>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <th scope="col" class="@(col.Align == OdsAlign.End ? "odc-rec-numeric" : null)"
                            style="@(col.Width is not null ? $"width:{col.Width}" : null)">
                            @HeaderFor(col)
                        </th>
                    }
                }
                <th scope="col" style="width:96px;text-align:right">Actions</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var (row, rowIndex) in VisibleRows.Select((r, i) => (r, i)))
            {
                var rk = RowKey(row);
                var detailId = $"{_detailIdPrefix}-{rowIndex}";
                var expanded = _openIds.Contains(rk);
                var editing = _editIds.Contains(rk);
                var cellCtx = new OdsRecordCellContext(expanded, editing, _savedIds.Contains(rk));
                var label = RowLabel?.Invoke(row);
                var busy = _busyKeys.Contains(rk);
                var headKey = RowHeader ?? Columns.FirstOrDefault()?.Key;
                <tr class="@RowClass(expanded, editing)" @onclick="@(() => OnRowClickAsync(rk, editing))">
                    @if (Leading is not null)
                    {
                        <td>@Leading(row)</td>
                    }
                    @foreach (var col in Columns)
                    {
                        var focusTarget = RowBusy is not null && col.Key == headKey;
                        @if (RowHeader is not null && col.Key == RowHeader)
                        {
                            <th scope="row" class="@CellClass(col)" id="@(focusTarget ? HeadIdFor(rk) : null)"
                                tabindex="@(focusTarget ? "-1" : null)" data-rt-focus="@(focusTarget ? "" : null)">
                                @col.Cell?.Invoke(row, cellCtx)
                            </th>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <td class="@CellClass(col)" id="@(focusTarget ? HeadIdFor(rk) : null)"
                                tabindex="@(focusTarget ? "-1" : null)" data-rt-focus="@(focusTarget ? "" : null)">
                                @col.Cell?.Invoke(row, cellCtx)
                            </td>
                        }
                    }
                    <td>
                        <div class="odc-rec-actions" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
                            @if (busy)
                            {
                                <span class="odc-rt-busy">
                                    <OdsSpinner Size="OdsSize.Sm" AriaLabel="@($"Saving {label ?? "row"}")" />
                                </span>
                            }
                            else if (Actions is not null && MenuItemsFor(row, rk, expanded, editing) is { } items)
                            {
                                <span id="@MenuIdFor(rk)" class="odc-rec-menu odc-rt-menu">
                                    <OdsMenu Items="@items" AriaLabel="Row actions" />
                                </span>
                            }
                            @if (CanExpand)
                            {
                                <button type="button" id="@ExpandIdFor(rk)" class="odc-rec-expand"
                                        aria-label="@ExpandLabel(expanded, label)" aria-expanded="@(expanded ? "true" : "false")"
                                        aria-controls="@(expanded ? detailId : null)"
                                        disabled="@editing" @onclick="@(() => ToggleRow(rk, fromMenu: false))" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
                                    <span class="material-icons odc-rec-chev @(expanded ? "open" : null)" aria-hidden="true">expand_more</span>
                                </button>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </td>
                </tr>
                @if (expanded)
                {
                    @* A named row (RowLabel) points its toggle at a labelled role="group" inside the panel — a
                       group, not a landmark, so a long table adds no regions; an unnamed one keeps pointing
                       at the detail row, as before. *@
                    <tr class="odc-rec-detail-row" id="@(label is null ? detailId : null)">
                        <td class="odc-rec-detail-cell" colspan="@ColSpan">
                            <div class="odc-rec-panel @(editing ? "editing" : null)" id="@PanelIdFor(rk)" tabindex="-1">
                                @if (label is not null)
                                {
                                    <div role="group" id="@detailId" aria-label="@($"Details for {label}")">
                                        @PanelBody(row, rk, editing)
                                    </div>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    @PanelBody(row, rk, editing)
                                }
                            </div>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                }
            }
            @* The first fetch renders OdsSkeletonRows shaped like this table's own columns, so the row
               layout (including right-aligned numeric cells) holds steady as real rows replace it. This
               is OdsListStatus's LoadingContent idea — the placeholder takes the shape of the thing
               loading — supplied centrally here rather than per page, because only the table knows its
               column count and alignment. A <tr> cannot live inside the status <td>, so loading is
               rendered here and OdsListStatus below keeps the error / empty states. *@
            @if (Loading)
            {
                @for (var i = 0; i < SkeletonRowCount; i++)
                {
                    <OdsSkeletonRow Columns="@ColSpan" Align="@SkeletonAlign" />
                }
            }
            @* One full-width status cell for the remaining pre-row states, so a page can neither invent
               its own dialect nor show the onboarding copy for a failed or over-filtered load. *@
            else if (Error || !VisibleRows.Any())
            {
                <tr class="odc-rec-detail-row">
                    <td colspan="@ColSpan" style="padding:0">
                        <OdsListStatus Error="Error" OnRetry="OnRetry" ErrorDescription="@ErrorDescription"
                                       IsEmpty="true" HasFilters="HasFilters" OnClearFilters="OnClearFilters"
                                       Noun="@Noun" EmptyIcon="@EmptyIcon" EmptyTitle="@EmptyTitle"
                                       EmptyDescription="@EmptyDescription" CreateAction="CreateAction" Empty="Empty" />
                    </td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

@code {
    private RenderFragment PanelBody(TRow row, object key, bool editing) =>
        editing && RenderEdit is not null ? RenderEdit(row, EditCtx(key)) : RenderDetail?.Invoke(row) ?? (_ => { });
}
